rationale:
Decision: split into 10 children — nine new theorems with fresh names idtp_fons_cc_psf_* and one reuse of the comparator-accepted Submission.dimred_cs_mi_withDensity_dilate at its byte-identical frozen type (already a registered dependency of this node).

Why split. The selected statement is a conjunction of seven independent clauses whose proofs use different tools: elementary dilation calculus for (1), (3), (4) and (7); Bochner integrals and barycenters for (2); dominated convergence, Riesz uniqueness and sequential compactness for (5); and the n-homogeneity of Hⁿ⌞f for (6). Five of the pieces are general facts that do not mention μ, and are stated that way: uniqueness of vague limits ((F6), step 5b); continuity of rescaled integrals in the parameters (5a); injectivity of the rescaling parametrization of a finite nonzero measure concentrated on B_2(0) (step 2); non-homogeneity of measures with finite positive mass (step 6); and vague_closed (5c), stated for any finite μ₀. This node is at depth 5 of 6, so the children are leaves. Each was therefore checked to be directly provable.

Children cannot use ambient_calculus. A child's Lean base is this node's dispatch commit d1625d76 (the bare contract plus handoffs), overlaid only with its own listed siblings (runtime _overlay_accepted_children). ambient_calculus is unaccepted and owned by the parent cone_class, so _existing_lean_name_problem forbids reusing its name here. Every 'AC (i)' fact the supplied proof cites (AC (2), (3), (8)) is a one-line consequence of dilation a s u = s⁻¹•(u − a), and is proved inline in the child proofs. This node keeps its registered dependencies; its assembly simply no longer needs ambient_calculus.

Coverage (supplied step → child): 0(a)–(c), 3 → total_mass; 0(d),(e), 1 → support; 2 → injective; 4 plus the membership test of 0(e) → domain_geometry; 5a → param_continuity; 5b (F6) → vague_unique; 5c → vague_closed; 6 → nonhomogeneous with the reused withdensity_dilate; 0(c)–(e), 7 → lower_bound. Departures are only presentational:
- support computes μ₀(B_σ(w)) directly with δ := 2 − ‖w‖, instead of going through μ₀^{0,1} = μ₀;
- vague_closed uses the test v ∈ G_{x,λ} ⟺ ‖x + λv‖ < 2 instead of the equivalent G_{x,λ} = B_{2/λ}(−x/λ);
- domain_geometry states the B_{1/λ}(0) inclusion of step 4 as closedBall 0 R ⊆ G_{x,λ} for λR ≤ 1.

Assembly (this node's own Lean proof): intro P n μ μ₀ z r hn hr hB0 hBinf hμ₀; obtain ⟨h0, hinf, hconc, hmass⟩ := total_mass P n μ μ₀ z r hr hB0 hBinf hμ₀; then
(1) support P n μ μ₀ z r hr hμ₀;
(2) injective P n μ₀ hn h0 hinf hconc;
(3) hmass;
(4) for admissible (x, λ), ⟨(domain_geometry P x λ hλ).2.1, ((domain_geometry P x λ hλ).2.2 hλ1 hx).1⟩;
(5) vague_closed P n μ₀ hinf;
(6) fun x λ f hλ hf => nonhomogeneous P n _ f hn (hmass x λ hλ).1 (hmass x λ hλ).2 hf;
(7) lower_bound P n μ μ₀ z r hr hμ₀.

Machine checks (toolchain v4.35.0-rc3, Mathlib 25730c7c; after import GMT.Ch07.Submission, in namespace GMT.Ch07 with the contract's opens):
- all ten lean_statements elaborate;
- the frozen parent type compiles from the child types stated as axioms. #print axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound and the seven directly used children;
- each of the nine new child types was proved outright, with its sibling inputs as axioms. A combined file proving all nine plus the assembly depends only on propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound and the accepted Submission.dimred_cs_mi_withDensity_dilate.

The runtime's own _dependency_problem and _topological accept the split. The only DAG lean_name match is the intended byte-identical accepted reuse. An independent reviewer judged all ten children correct and complete; its four wording suggestions were applied.
